baseline 146 tests pass; 235 mutations, 235 caught, 0 survived, 0 not applicable. One behaviour is broken at a time in a scratch copy of scripts/eng, scripts/collab and infra/gitlab-engineering/{rehearsal,settings,ci,m2.sh}: the plan, the arguments, every refusal, the allowlists of AWS and of writes (and the new guard on main), the preflight reads of the fleet group and the seed self-test, the seed (manifest, blob id, diff, address), the three controls with their statuses, the baseline and the job script, the parsers, every threshold and verdict of A1, A2, A3, A4 and A8, the order of the waves, cleanup, redaction, the last resort, exit codes. The first pass over the new mutations (236 in the harness) left 4 alive: a 3xx status counted as data (the cases now include 302), a NEGCTL-INFO line read by the failure parser (a look-alike line is now in the case), the fleet read message left unredacted (a unit case of fleetReadProblems now pins it), and one mutation that could not change behaviour (a detail added to a control that passed, which cannot have a detail): it was removed from the harness. The harness lists its own mistakes (NOOP, AMBIGUOUS, INVALID, CRASH, HUNG count as not caught).

